         }
      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "SQL::Abstract versions from 1.90_01 before 2.000001_04 for Perl skip the injection_guard check for function names given with -func.\n\ninjection_guard is documented to apply to every function name, but only the { -name => ... } shorthand goes through it. The explicit { -func => [ $name, ... ] } form puts $name into the SQL unchecked.\n\nAn application that relies on injection_guard to reject an untrusted function name passed with -func allows SQL injection.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
